hke|n|One of the two points of an orbit, as of a planet or satellite, which are at the greatest and least distance from the central body, corresponding to the aphelion and perihelion of a planet, or to the apogee and perigee of the moon. The more distant is called the higher apsis; the other, the lower apsis; and the line joining them, the line of apsides. ; In a curve referred to polar coordinates, any point for which the radius vector is a maximum or minimum. ; Same as Apse.	a:6otm,77,4~6otm,77,4	N:98ew,87,2;59kk,51,10~59kk,51,10;98ew,87,2
